Usage: nimbu channels entries update --channel=STRING --entry=STRING [<assignments> ...] [flags]

Update entry

Arguments:
  [<assignments> ...]    Inline assignments (e.g. title=Hello,
                         fields.teaser=Text)

Flags:
      --channel=STRING    Channel ID or slug
      --entry=STRING      Entry ID or slug
      --locale=STRING     Content locale for localized field writes. Reads are
                          per-locale (one GET per locale; the API returns no
                          translations map for entries). Non-localized fields
                          ignore --locale.
      --file=STRING       Read entry JSON from file (use - for stdin)

Global Flags:
  -h, --help              Show context-sensitive help.
      --env=STRING        Named project environment (overrides site and API URL)
      --site=STRING       Site ID or subdomain, else nimbu.yml site
                          ($NIMBU_SITE)
      --json              Output JSON to stdout ($NIMBU_JSON)
      --plain             Output stable TSV to stdout ($NIMBU_PLAIN)
      --verbose           Enable verbose logging
      --debug             Enable debug logging (HTTP traces)
      --version           Print version and exit

Examples:
  # Change one field
  nimbu channels entries update --channel blog --entry welcome title=Welcome

  # Typed values use :=
  nimbu channels entries update --channel blog --entry welcome published:=true

  # Update the English translation from stdin
  echo '{"title":"Welcome"}' | nimbu channels entries update \
    --channel blog --entry welcome --locale en --file -

Run "nimbu channels entries update --help-all" for all flags.
